{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.channelScale_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.channelScale_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L186-L192","doc":"And the scale is mirror-invariant: it does not see the charge, which is\ncorrect for a nuclear radius and is the one place the channel assignment's\n\"reversed parity\" is the *right* way round. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.cubed_scale_is_the_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.cubed_scale_is_the_channel","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L177-L184","doc":"Such a scale's cube is affine in `A` with slope `10` — extensive, hence its\nroot grows as `A^{1/3}`. No hyperbolic volume is required anywhere: the count\nchannel is defined for every braid word, degenerate or not, which is what makes\nit available where `atom-branch-hyperbolicity` measured **0 of 40** branch\nclosures hyperbolic across p, n and the deuteron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.IsChannelScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.IsChannelScale","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L171-L175","doc":"A scale `s` **is** the Coulomb-channel length scale exactly when its cube is\nthat channel. Purely definitional — recorded so the downstream archimedean\nspecialisation has a generic statement to instantiate, rather than introducing\n`Real.rpow` on this side of the wall. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.quadratic_escapes_linear_exclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.quadratic_escapes_linear_exclusion","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L144-L162","doc":"**Located, not contradicted.** For every choice of linear coefficients there\nis a `Z` at which the linear form misses `Z(Z-1)` — that is\n`CrossingCountAffine`'s content — while the quadratic form matches at *every*\n`Z`, with the coefficient fixed in advance. Over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.counts_determine_protonPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.counts_determine_protonPairs","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L128-L137","doc":"Stated as a determination: the two counts fix the proton-pair number. Any\n`(A, Z)` and `(A', Z')` agreeing on both channels agree on `Z(Z-1)`. Over a ring\nwhere `16 ≠ 0`; `ℤ` and `ℚ` qualify. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.protonPairs_from_counts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.protonPairs_from_counts","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L117-L126","doc":"**The point of this file.** `Z(Z-1)` is an exact quadratic function of the\ncrossing counts, with no hypotheses and no division:\n\n    16·Z(Z-1) = (n₊ - n₋)·(n₊ - n₋ - 4)\n\n`CrossingCountAffine.no_crossing_combination_is_protonPairs` excludes the\n**linear** combinations only; this is what lies immediately outside that class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.strongChannel_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.strongChannel_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L110-L113","doc":"The signed channel is `4Z` — it carries all of the charge dependence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.coulombChannel_extensive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.coulombChannel_extensive","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L104-L108","doc":"The unsigned (mirror-invariant) channel is **extensive**: `10A - 2`,\ndepending on `A` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.protonPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.protonPairs","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L101-L102","doc":"The number of proton pairs, doubled to stay division-free: `Z(Z-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.nMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.nMinus","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Negative crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.nPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoulombFromCrossingCounts.nPlus","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CoulombFromCrossingCounts.lean#L94-L96","doc":"Positive crossings of the `A`-nucleon atom braid, `Z` protons. Measured in\n`level3_em_channel_parity_probe` on 12 nuclei to `A = 39`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}